Question 3: OpenClaw Installation (Setup and Onboarding - Complete Configuration)

Ans--  OpenClaw is an open-source AI agent framework that allows users to create and run AI agents locally. It supports multiple AI model providers and provides a secure environment for AI agent execution.

Installation and Configuration Steps

Step 1: Install WSL2 and Ubuntu
Install WSL2 on Windows.
Open Ubuntu to perform the installation.

Step 2: Install OpenClaw
Run the official installation command in the Ubuntu terminal.

```bash
curl -fsSL https://openclaw.ai/install.sh | bash
```

Step 3: Complete Onboarding
After installation, OpenClaw automatically:

Creates the workspace.
Configures the local Gateway.
Initializes the default agent.
Starts the Gateway service.

Step 4: Configure the Model Provider
During onboarding:

Select OpenRouter as the model provider.
Choose OpenRouter API Key authentication.
Enter the OpenRouter API key.
Keep the default model as:
openrouter/auto

Step 5: Finish the Setup

After configuration, OpenClaw successfully:
Connected to the OpenRouter model provider.
Started the Gateway service.
Completed the onboarding process.
Prepared the workspace for running AI agents.